| **Lack of rotation** – Changing a secret requires updating the file on every host and redeploying the service. |
| **No audit trail** – Plain files do not provide versioned access logs that a managed secrets store can offer. |
| **Plain‑text at rest** – The file lives on disk unencrypted, which may violate compliance requirements (PCI‑DSS, HIPAA, GDPR, etc.). |
| **Inconsistent environments** – Different staging/production clusters must each have a copy of the file, increasing the chance of mismatched or stale values. |

