## 4️⃣ Checklist for Ongoing Development

| ✅ | Item |
|----|------|
| **A01 – Broken Access Control** | Add authentication, role checks, and verify that every protected endpoint uses the auth middleware. |
| **A02 – Cryptographic Failures** | Enforce TLS 1.2+, store secrets (JWT, DB passwords) in env vars or secret manager, use strong hashing for passwords. |
| **A03 – Injection** | Validate & sanitize all external input (query params, body, headers). Use prepared statements/ORM parameterization. |
| **A04 – Insecure Design** | Document threat model; keep security considerations in design reviews. |
| **A05 – Security Misconfiguration** | Keep `helmet` defaults, disable `x-powered-by`, set `trust proxy` correctly when behind a reverse proxy. |
| **A06 – Vulnerable & Outdated Components** | Run `npm audit` CI step, auto‑merge Dependabot PRs, pin exact versions. |
| **A07 – XSS** | If you ever render HTML, enable CSP, escape output, use templating engines with auto‑escaping. |
| **A08 – Insecure Deserialization** | Avoid `eval`, `JSON.parse` on untrusted data that later becomes code; prefer a whitelist of allowed fields. |
| **A09 – Using Components with Known Vulnerabilities** | Same as A06 – remain on top of dependency advisories. |
| **A10 – Insufficient Logging & Monitoring** | Ship logs to a central system, monitor for anomalies (rate‑limit hits, auth failures). |

---

### Final Thoughts

- The current code is **functionally safe** because it processes no user input, but it **lacks the baseline security scaffolding** that any production‑grade Express app should have.
- By integrating the middleware shown above **today**, you future‑proof the codebase: new routes (POST/PUT/DELETE) will automatically inherit validation, rate‑limiting, HTTPS, and logging.
- Keep the **security checklist** as part of your pull‑request review template—this ensures every new change is vetted against the OWASP Top 10.

Feel free to ask for deeper dives into any specific area (e.g., JWT implementation, CSP tuning, CI‑pipeline hardening, etc.). Happy hardening!

